In \textbf{1789}, the \textbf{Estates-General} was called to address France's financial crisis. This led to the formation of the National Assembly, which took the \textbf{Tennis Court Oath} in \textbf{June} to establish a new constitution. In \textbf{July}, the \textbf{Storming of the Bastille} marked the beginning of the revolution.
In \textbf{August}, the National Assembly adopted the \textbf{Declaration of the Rights of Man}, which proclaimed liberty, equality, and fraternity. The \textbf{Constitution of 1791} was established in \textbf{September}, which limited the power of the monarchy and created a constitutional monarchy.
In \textbf{1793}, King Louis XVI was \textbf{executed}, and the revolution entered a more radical phase. Finally, in \textbf{1799}, Napoleon Bonaparte took power in a coup d'état and established the Napoleonic Empire.
In the end, it led to the creation of the Republic.
